WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:04.148
Unit twenty-one. Spotting Phishing Messages!

2
00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:10.076
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:14.081
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:14.131 --> 00:00:18.827
Today we learn about Spotting Phishing Messages. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:23.273
Phishing. Say it with me. Phishing!

6
00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:30.840
Message. Say it with me. Message!

7
00:00:34.388 --> 00:00:38.010
Link. Say it with me. Link!

8
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.197
Urgent. Say it with me. Urgent!

9
00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:52.448
Prize. Say it with me. Prize!

10
00:00:55.986 --> 00:01:00.038
Password. Say it with me. Password!

11
00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:07.360
Scam. Say it with me. Scam!

12
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.727
Report. Say it with me. Report!

13
00:01:18.202 --> 00:01:30.523
Phishing is a scam message that tries to trick you. It may sound urgent or promise a prize and ask you to click a link or share a password. I do not click — I report it to an adult.

14
00:01:30.573 --> 00:01:34.148
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:35.169 --> 00:01:40.490
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.690
Link!

17
00:01:42.624 --> 00:01:48.006
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.056 --> 00:01:49.206
Scam!

19
00:01:50.202 --> 00:01:56.662
Did you know? Real companies will never ask you to send your password by message or email!

20
00:01:56.712 --> 00:01:59.078
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:00.101 --> 00:02:08.563
Think and answer. What signs show a message might be phishing?

22
00:02:08.613 --> 00:02:09.763
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.772 --> 00:02:16.870
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.034
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

